    <!-- About -->
    <string name="settings_section_about">About</string>
    <string name="settings_section_open_source">Open source &amp; privacy</string>
    <string name="about_paragraph_1">This is a completely unofficial app, made by a JavaZone fan whose hobby project has taken on a life of its own. The goal is to explore new technologies in my spare time, and to play around with AI.</string>
    <string name="about_paragraph_2">Yes, the app is mostly vibe-coded: the AI assistants have done the typing while I stood behind them saying &#8220;Looks good!&#8221;. Most of the time it works surprisingly well. The rest of the time I&#8217;m glad this is only a hobby project.</string>
    <string name="about_paragraph_3">Without JavaZone and JavaBin&#8217;s open APIs, this would just have been a good idea with no content. Thanks for sharing!</string>
    <string name="about_paragraph_4">Enjoying the app and want to support its development? I&#8217;d appreciate a small contribution &#8211; either via Vipps or &#8220;Buy Me a Coffee&#8221;:</string>
    <string name="about_open_source_body">The code is open, and suggestions, bug reports and pull requests are welcome.</string>
    <string name="about_open_source_link">github.com/olavbg/JavaZone</string>
    <string name="about_privacy_paragraph">Your favorites and settings are stored only on your device, and no analytics or tracking are used. The app fetches the conference schedule from the public JavaZone API.</string>

